---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import StructureFacts from "../../components/StructureFacts.astro";
import SetStructureDemo from "../../components/SetStructureDemo.astro";
import TermCallout from "../../components/TermCallout.astro";
import { twoPSetTerm } from "../../lib/atlas/standalone-terms";
import "../../styles/set-lesson.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="TwoPSet"
  description="Alice retires the old Eagle Creek beacon, but its permanent tombstone blocks Bob's replacement."
  territory="Structures"
  sheetTitle="TwoPSet"
>
  <article class="set-lesson">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="territory-label">Structures</p>
      <h1>TwoPSet</h1>
      <p class="structure-summary">
        Alice has found that the old Eagle Creek beacon is gone. The ranger
        needs its name removed even if Carol later receives a stale copy of the
        original report.
      </p>
    </header>

    <StructureFacts
      family="CRDT"
      model="State-based two-phase set"
      updates="Add, then remove permanently"
      merge="Union the addition set and the removal set."
      delivery="Removal survives repeated and out-of-order delivery"
      bestFor="Membership where retirement must be final"
      cost="Retain additions and permanent tombstones"
    />

    <section aria-labelledby="retire-beacon-title">
      <h2 id="retire-beacon-title">Alice retires the old beacon</h2>
      <p>
        The hikers keep one grow-only set of additions and another grow-only
        set of removals. Alice puts <code>Eagle Creek</code> in the removal
        set. Carol can receive the old addition afterward, but the removal
        still wins.
      </p>
      <p>
        A <dfn><a href="/glossary/#twopset">TwoPSet</a></dfn> considers a
        value present only when it appears in the addition set and not in the
        removal set.
      </p>
      <TermCallout {...twoPSetTerm} />
      <figure>
        <table aria-label="Eagle Creek TwoPSet state">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Record</th><th scope="col">Members</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Additions</th><td>Eagle Creek</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Removals</th><td>Eagle Creek</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Visible set</th><td>empty</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <figcaption>The removal record remains after the visible member disappears.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <pre aria-label="TwoPSet membership rule"><code>members = additions - removals</code></pre>
    </section>

    <SetStructureDemo
      kind="two-p-set"
      title="Race retirement against replacement"
      description="Alice retires Eagle Creek while Bob reports the same name again. The permanent tombstone must win at all three notebooks."
      rule="Union additions and removals; removal wins forever."
      raceLabel="Race Alice's retirement and Bob's report"
    />

    <section aria-labelledby="replacement-title">
      <h2 id="replacement-title">Bob finds the replacement</h2>
      <p>
        The next morning, Bob finds a new beacon at Eagle Creek. Its name is
        the same, so he tries to add <code>Eagle Creek</code> again. The old
        removal record still excludes that value.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is the cost of permanent removal. A TwoPSet cannot distinguish two
        installations that use the same value. The next set gives every add
        its own identity, so Alice can remove the old beacon while Bob's new
        beacon survives.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="notes-title">
      <h2 id="notes-title">Sources and implementation</h2>
      <p>
        Watershed's{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/tylerbutler/watershed/blob/4a8739323ee491f353fcaa8ccfb0488419c1cd43/src/watershed/two_p_set_kernel.gleam">TwoPSet kernel</a>
        {" "}stores additions and removals as two monotonic sets.
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="structure-next" aria-label="Continue through set structures">
      <a href="/structures/g-set/">Back to GSet</a>
      <a href="/structures/sets/">Browse set family</a>
      <a href="/structures/observed-remove-set/">Continue to observed-remove set</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
